(a) Generally. Every person required to procure a license under the provisions of this article shall submit an application for such license to the city clerk, which application shall conform to the requirements of this section.
(b) Form. Each application shall be a written statement upon forms provided by the city clerk.
(c) Contents. Each application shall contain the following information:
(1) The name and home address of the applicant if an individual, or the home office address if a corporation or partnership;
(2) The place where the proposed business is to be located;
(3) The kind of business to be carried on;
(4) The name and home address of each partner, if a partnership;
(5) The names and home addresses of the officers and directors, if a corporation;
(6) A complete record of all arrests and convictions against the applicant and every partner, officer, or director of the applicant for violations of any laws and ordinances of the city, state, or federal government; and
(7) Such additional information which the city clerk or council may find reasonably necessary to the fair administration of this article.
(d) Verification. Each application shall be sworn to by the applicant if an individual, or by a partner if a partnership, or by an officer if a corporation.
(e) Confidentiality. All information furnished or secured under the authority of this section shall be kept in strict confidence of the city clerk, shall not be subject to public inspection, and shall be utilized solely by the officers of the city responsible for administering the provisions of this article.
(f) False statements. False statements on any application for a license shall be grounds for denial or immediate revocation of such license.
(Code 1988, § 12-30)
